Keith, you are right, I apologize for not giving a reproducible example. I will not make that mistake the next time.

Your examples were very helpful, and led me to the answer. I do not have raw data but have a covariance matrix in machine readable form. My issue was that the upper triangle was empty. Thus, I needed to copy/transpose my lower triangle to my upper triangle (and save the row names as the column names). m[upper.tri(m)] <- t(m)[upper.tri(m)]

This did the trick, and I did not need to apply the getCov() function.

Thank you again for your answers, I would have moved on otherwise!

Best.

