Ashish

lavaan doent impute data, to do imputations you have to set up with the runMI function.

It seems they are both using Full Information Maximum Likelihood (FIML), this never generates imputed values.

The main issue seems to show in the standard error for the regressions for the dummy variables.

I think that this due to some error inputing the data into R, because Mplus and lavaan are basically working different data. You can see this in the baseline model chi-square 421.1 for Mplus and 1428.5 for lavaan. Is is bases on a model of only variances, so, this is telling that the variances are different en each data set.

would recommend you to look at your data and see if there are some weird values in R. For example, maybe some -99 are still there

