Hello Drew and Terrence,

I came across a similar issue and a friend found me a solution.

The problem was the following: I had a MGM with 4 groups and a latent variable with three indicators. I wanted the loadings of one factor to be equal in group 2 and 3, but estimated freely in groups 1 and 4. The group.partial() command covers only releasing the parameter in all groups. Thus, I had a look at the tutorial. But this specific issue seems not to be covered there. Neither did I find any reference among the other resources offered on the lavaan-page.

With labeling I get equality constraints (check):
Deter =~ c(m1,m1,m1,m1)*rskminor

Coming from an Mplus-background I was thinking in defaults and thus wanting to override it with "NA". To quote from the tutorial: "multiply it with NA, as a hint to lavaan that the value of this parameter is still unknown". That's what I thought the solution ought to be:
Deter =~ c(NA,m1,m1,NA)*rskminor
But that doesn't work.

The final solution was to assign a specific label to each parameter I want to estimate
Deter =~ c(m2,m1,m1,m3)*rskminor

Maybe an equal example could be added to the tutorial?

Best,
Georg

