> Coming from an Mplus-background I was thinking in defaults and thus wanting to override it with "NA". To quote from the tutorial: "multiply it with NA, as a hint to lavaan that the value of this parameter is still unknown". That's what I thought the solution ought to be:
> Deter =~ c(NA,m1,m1,NA)*rskminor
> But that doesn't work.

That is not the way to use NAs.  NAs (for "free this parameter") are only to be mixed with fixed values, such as

Deter =~ c(NA, 1, 1, NA)*rskminor

>  The final solution was to assign a specific label to each parameter I want to estimate
> Deter =~ c(m2,m1,m1,m3)*rskminor

This is the correct way to set equality constraints on a subset of freely estimated parameters.

> Maybe an equal example could be added to the tutorial?

http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html

See sections in the second half of the page: "Fixing parameters in some groups, but not all" and "Constraining a single parameter to be equal across groups".

