>      >     For now (using dev 0.6-1), just adding a cluster=  argument
>     is not
>      >     enough. You must adapt your syntax and add a level: 1 and
>     level: 2
>      >     section.
>      >
>      >     For example:
>      >
>      >     myModel <- '
>      >           level: 1
>      >                fw =~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4
>      >           level: 2
>      >                fb =~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4
>      >     '
>      >
>      >     If you have no model for the between level (level 2), create a
>      >     saturated
>      >     model:
>      >
>      >        myModel <- '
>      >           level: 1
>      >                fw =~ y1 + y2 + y3 + y4
>      >           level: 2
>      >                y1 ~~ y2 + y3 + y4
>      >                y2 ~~ y3 + y4
>      >                y3 ~~ y4
>      >     '
>      >
>      >     This will not be needed any longer in a next update of 0.6-1,
>     because
>      >     this will be the default behavior.
>      >
